# Witness: a legend that is not the nine marks

This legend publishes a tenth mark and drops one of the nine. The first attempt read the
legend with the same capped regex it used for the body, so a tenth mark was invisible to the
equality check that was supposed to catch it.

## 1. How To Use This File

### Evidence verdicts - set by the author, about evidence

| Mark | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `[MET]` | Demonstrated. |
| `[PART]` | Partly demonstrated. |
| `[UNMET]` | Not discharged. |
| `[N/A]` | Not claimed at this milestone. |
| `[WAIVED]` | A tenth mark, which the nine do not contain. |

### Review verdicts - set by the reviewer, about their own reading

| Mark | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `[ ]` | Not yet reviewed. |
| `[A]` | Accepted as stated. |
| `[C]` | Accepted with a condition. |
| `[R]` | Rejected. |

## 2. Something Else

`[?]` is never published above, so the legend is short of the nine as well as over them.
